lisa-design:
- OpenAPI 3.0.3 with oapi-codegen v2.7.2 (go.mod tool): 3.1 needs v2.8+, whose runtime (>= v1.4) forces Echo >= v4.15.1, outside the allow-list (v4.13.x like api).
- Webhooks and ops routes are documented under their own servers and excluded from server/client generation (exclude-tags); routes_test checks the mounted routes are exactly the public /api/v1 operations.
- v1alpha1 types are mapped with x-go-type (aliases), never copied; spec_test reflects over the Go types to catch drift (fields, required vs omitzero, enums).
- Package api embeds openapi.yaml + examples: one copy for tests, factory-mock and the generators.
- Registration credentials are headers (X-Factory-Join-Token, X-Factory-Owner-Token) so they are real security schemes; scheduler-and-pools.md updated.
- vacuum runs via go run at a pinned version (not a go.mod tool: its dependency tree would move shared deps); recommended rules minus three justified in api/vacuum.yaml.
- Added the Cancelling task phase and GET /runs/{id}/transcript (gzip JSON Lines, same as PUT): both were used by RT/WEB LLDs but missing from the contract.

